            <ArticleTitle>The relationship between left ventricular shape and QT interval dispersion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>641-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Left ventricular geometry is suspected to affect heterogeneity of myocardial repolarization; therefore, it is plausible but unproven that increased sphericity of the left ventricle is associated with greater QT interval dispersion. In 60 patients with dilated cardiomyopathy with left ventricular ejection fraction &lt; or = 30%, we found that spherical distortion of the left ventricle was associated with increased QT dispersion, implying increased heterogeneity of myocardial repolarization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
